nterested parties to create and establish a successful public transit\ninitiative for the Peconic Bay region. Bringing the stakeholders and\ncommunity members together in the development of the plan will ensure\nan open and comprehensive decision making process.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :  2013-14 S.1859/A.1461; 2011-12\nS.1459A/A.1412A; 2009-10 S.3181B/A.6743B; 2007-08 S.1235/A.1735;\n2005-06 S.6670/A.9784.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : To be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :  This act shall take effect immediately and shall\nremain in full force and effect until December 31, 2026 when upon such\ndate the provisions of this act shall expire and be deemed repealed.\n",
